rule: TEST_DISABLED
title: removing the if around an existing pytest.skip leaves it firing everywhere
origin: #196 183.2 — THREATMODEL 54's other half. The call keeps its name, so no marker is added, and with no guard left nothing was evaluated; v0.5.0 passes it
=== before: tests/test_quota.py ===
import sys

import pytest

from app import remaining


def test_weighted_quota():
    if sys.version_info < (3, 9):
        pytest.skip("needs 3.9")

    assert remaining(10, [("get", 1), ("bulk", 4)]) == 5
=== after: tests/test_quota.py ===
import sys

import pytest

from app import remaining


def test_weighted_quota():
    pytest.skip("needs 3.9")

    assert remaining(10, [("get", 1), ("bulk", 4)]) == 5
